When Should You Talk to a Doctor?

If your periods are extremely heavy and you regularly experience weakness, dizziness, unusual tiredness, or shortness of breath, it is important to speak with a healthcare professional. Heavy menstrual bleeding can sometimes contribute to iron deficiency or anaemia.

Overall, there is no complicated “period diet” that everyone needs to follow. Focus on nutritious meals, enough fluids, iron-rich foods, protein, fruits, vegetables, and whole grains. Combined with good menstrual hygiene and suitable period products, these simple habits can help you manage your period more comfortably.
